g an easier problem:\n\n$$\n52+502\n$$\n\nNext, we carry out the addition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n52+502=554.\n$$\n\nHowever, since our answer must be negative, we need to change the sign of the answer above. \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n-52-502=-554.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5b6c445a-2d2b-5c07-9254-68e2530c6900"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5b6c445a-2d2b-5c07-9254-68e2530c6900" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b6c445a-2d2b-5c07-9254-68e2530c6900" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-df160c1a-bb36-5116-98e1-b396393bba4e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-df160c1a-bb36-5116-98e1-b396393bba4e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df160c1a-bb36-5116-98e1-b396393bba4e" :answer/id #uuid "df160c1a-bb36-5116-98e1-b396393bba4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-554" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9c8a9030-cacb-58cf-b9f4-8070b5c94b71" :question/id #uuid "9c8a9030-cacb-58cf-b9f4-8070b5c94b71" :question/math-academy-id "q-101205" :question/problem "$-50-50=$" :question/worked-solution "The answer will be negative since $-50$ is negative, and we're subtracting $50$ from it.\n\nWe start by solving an easier problem:\n\n$$\n50+50\n$$\n\nNext, we carry out the addition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\text{ }1\\,\\,\\,\\, &  &  \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n50+50=100.\n$$\n\nHowever, since our answer must be negative, we need to change the sign of the answer above. \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n-50-50=-100.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ff6a6180-085e-5ffe-b9ad-66f08fe39c55"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ff6a6180-085e-5ffe-b9ad-66f08fe39c55" :answer-field/id #uuid "ff6a6180-085e-5ffe-b9ad-66f08fe39c55" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f3f17c92-1c6a-531e-bd19-4c0067babf66" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f3f17c92-1c6a-531e-bd19-4c0067babf66" "answer-091ad877-b264-5917-bf6d-f1db6c50ebec" "answer-a10a3162-5364-5606-b7f0-7ffb109b5817" "answer-f8ec62df-ddec-5e08-a324-b6fbbccf22bf" "answer-09186b49-e45c-58a1-9a92-4f5b91877f03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f3f17c92-1c6a-531e-bd19-4c0067babf66" :answer/id #uuid "f3f17c92-1c6a-531e-bd19-4c0067babf66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-100" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-091ad877-b264-5917-bf6d-f1db6c50ebec" :answer/id #uuid "091ad877-b264-5917-bf6d-f1db6c50ebec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a10a3162-5364-5606-b7f0-7ffb109b5817" :answer/id #uuid "a10a3162-5364-5606-b7f0-7ffb109b5817" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f8ec62df-ddec-5e08-a324-b6fbbccf22bf" :answer/id #uuid "f8ec62df-ddec-5e08-a324-b6fbbccf22bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "100" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09186b49-e45c-58a1-9a92-4f5b91877f03" :answer/id #uuid "09186b49-e45c-58a1-9a92-4f5b91877f03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-30d2f725-3679-5a9b-883a-cea7d083fba5" :question/id #uuid "30d2f725-3679-5a9b-883a-cea7d083fba5" :question/math-academy-id "q-174112" :question/problem "$-30-215=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The answer will be negative since $-30$ is negative, and we're subtracting $215$ from it.\n\nWe start by solving an easier problem:\n\n$$\n30+215\n$$\n\nNext, we carry out the addition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n30+215=245.\n$$\n\nHowever, since our answer must be negative, we need to change the sign of the answer above. \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n-30-215=-245.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-58e6334d-cd43-53c2-9b4a-62c34ae1c218"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-58e6334d-cd43-53c2-9b4a-62c34ae1c218" :answer-field/id #uuid "58e6334d-cd43-53c2-9b4a-62c34ae1c218" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-de7992fc-8491-5431-925e-36f035864a37" :answer-field/choices ["answer-de7992fc-8491-5431-925e-36f035864a37"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-de7992fc-8491-5431-925e-36f035864a37" :answer/id #uuid "de7992fc-8491-5431-925e-36f035864a37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-245" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180770 :tutorial/content "When we subtract a positive number from a negative number, we move towards the left on the number line. \n\nFor example, let's consider the following subtraction problem:\n\n$$\n-1 - 6\n$$\n\nTo subtract $6$ from $-1,$ we start at $-1$ on the number line and move $6$ places to the left.\n\n![](images/27/27f1ec50826854059d1794b7f449704e084688437f7fecd64ff23de65a081343.png)\n\nWhen we do this, we land at $-7.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n-1-6 = -7.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180771 :tutorial/content "It is impractical to use number lines to subtract large numbers. \n\nHowever, a neat trick makes subtracting a positive number from a negative number very easy!\n\nAs an example, let's consider the following subtraction problem:\n\n$$\n-37 - 52\n$$\n\nThe answer will be *negative* since $-37$ is negative, and we're subtracting $52$ from it.\n\nWe start by solving an easier problem: adding their absolute values. In other words, we need to figure out\n\n$$\n37+52 .\n$$\n\nCarrying out the addition gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,7\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n37+52 = 89.\n$$\n\nHowever, since our answer must be negative, we need to change the sign of the answer above. \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n-37 - 52 = -89.\n$$\n\nAnd that's it! \n\nLet's use this technique to solve a problem with three-digit numbers." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179871 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
